  "//_defaultMode": "acceptEdits = reads/edits within allowed paths happen freely; Bash commands NOT in the allow list above still prompt. This is the safer default. If /jarvis:advance is still stopping you for things you don't want to review one-by-one, the fix is almost always to ADD the specific command to permissions.allow above — see '//_why_this_is_wide'. Switching defaultMode to 'bypassPermissions' removes ALL prompts including ask/deny enforcement for permission checks — this defeats the purpose of the deny list above (rm -rf, curl, credentials reads all stop being blocked) and should only be used in a fully disposable sandboxed environment, never on a machine with real credentials or an unbacked-up working tree.",
